  "answer": "Requests normally determines Content-Length while preparing the request, not in HTTPAdapter.send. PreparedRequest.prepare_body calls super_len(body). For strings, it first encodes them as UTF-8; otherwise it checks, in order: __len__(), a .len attribute, the file descriptor size via fileno()/fstat(), or—when available—seeks to the end and restores the original position. The returned value is total_length minus the current read position. If a positive length is found, Requests sets Content-Length to that value. For a body whose length cannot be determined, it uses Transfer-Encoding: chunked instead. In HTTPAdapter.send, chunked is selected only when the body is not None and Content-Length is absent. During most redirects, Requests removes Content-Length, Content-Type, and Transfer-Encoding and clears the body before preparing the redirected request again; temporary and permanent redirects preserve the body and headers.",
